In this JSON object, I have defined a single rule with a trigger that checks if the user input contains the string "specter". If this trigger is true, the rule has a weight of 100, which means it is a strong match and will cause me to grant access. If the trigger is false, I will default to the "lock out" action.

Note that the weights in this example are arbitrary and can be adjusted based on the specific requirements of the system. In general, weights are used to prioritize rules and determine which one to apply when multiple rules match. A higher weight indicates a stronger match, while a lower weight indicates a weaker match.

